[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186172039,
      "id": "fd092f29-08bf-5425-88a4-8cba4f0a31c8",
      "title": "Identifying Quadrants Where a Slope Field Is Positive or Negative"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e2a3cefe-3f63-5419-b3f3-7649602dc854",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=5x$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** At every point in the third quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive\n- **II.** At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative\n- **III.** At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we define $f(x,y)=5x.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0.$ In each open quadrant, $x$ has a fixed nonzero sign. The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/generated/signs-pnnp-zero-x.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the third quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the third quadrant.\n\n- Statement II is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement III is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "cfaeddb8-5dc9-55a8-961b-e9d1b313d4ff",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
